  "lapsed_date": "30/10/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed variation of Clauses 2 and 3 of Schedule F of the Section 106 Agreement associated with planning permission ref. 2011/01753/FUL would remove the requirement for a public access route between Sulivan Road and Carnwath Road and the courtyard area between East Court and West Court. These were secured as a significant public benefit of the parent permission and continue to serve a useful planning purpose by contributing to pedestrian permeability, accessibility, connectivity and public realm quality. The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the obligation can no longer be complied with, that circumstances have materially changed such that the obligation is no longer necessary, or that the purposes of the obligation would be equally well served by the proposed modification. The proposal would therefore result in the unjustified loss of a significant public benefit of the original permission. This is contrary to policies DC1 and T1 of the Local Plan (2018) and policies D5, D6 and D8 of the London Plan (2021) and is accordingly unacceptable."
  ],
